." $NetBSD$
.Dd March 10, 2026
.Dt CELLUI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cellui
.Nd interactive terminal UI for managing cellmgr cells
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility provides an interactive
.Xr curses 3
interface for operating cells managed by
.Xr cellmgr 8
and
.Xr cellctl 8 .
It shows configured and running cells in a table, displays per-cell details,
and allows common lifecycle actions from the keyboard.
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
refreshes its view every 4 seconds.
Status data is built from configured cells in
.Ev CELL_DATA_DIR
and runtime data from
.Cm cellctl list
and
.Cm cellctl stats .
.Sh KEY BINDINGS
In normal mode, the following keys are available:
.Bl -tag -width "enter"
.It Cm j , Cm k , KEY_UP , KEY_DOWN
Move selection down or up.
.It KEY_PPAGE , KEY_NPAGE
Move one page up or down.
.It Cm r
Refresh immediately.
.It Cm f
Cycle filter mode:
.Dq all ,
.Dq running ,
or
.Dq stopped .
.It Cm m
Rotate color theme.
.It Cm enter
Open an interactive shell inside the selected cell using
.Cm cellctl exec .
.It Cm s , Cm x , Cm t
Start, stop, or restart the selected cell using
.Xr cellmgr 8 .
.It Cm a , Cm z , Cm y
Start all, stop all, or restart all configured cells.
.It Cm e
Open the selected cell configuration via
.Cm cellmgr config .
.It Cm :
Enter command mode.
.It Cm q , Ctrl-C
Quit.
.El
.Pp
In command mode,
.Nm
shows a
.Dq cellmgr
prompt prefix.
Typed input is parsed as shell-style words and executed as
.Cm cellmgr Ar args ... .
Press
.Cm enter
to run the command, or
.Cm Esc
to cancel.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width CELLMGR_CONF
.It Ev CELLMGR_CONF
Path to a
.Xr cellmgr 8
configuration file.
If unset,
.Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf
is used.
The
.Ev CELL_DATA_DIR
assignment from that file controls where configured cells are discovered.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/cellmgr/cells/name/cell.conf
.It Pa /etc/cellmgr.conf
Default
.Xr cellmgr 8
configuration file.
.It Pa /var/cellmgr/cells
Default configured cell data directory.
.It Pa /var/cellmgr/cells/name/cell.conf
Per-cell configuration read for display metadata.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cellctl 8 ,
.Xr cellmgr 8 ,
.Xr curses 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Nx 11 .
